---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Bare Metal Press is and how it publishes.">
  <Hero title="About" em={2.319} compact />

  <section class="wrap intro">
    <h2>Down to the metal</h2>
    <p>
      We are a group of researchers and analysts running an independent
      project: training material across multiple disciplines, written by people
      who work in them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most instructional material stops at the surface. It explains the
      interface and leaves the machinery untouched, which holds up until the
      reader meets a problem the manual did not anticipate. We write the other
      kind — the account that goes all the way down, so what remains afterwards
      is understanding rather than a procedure to repeat.
    </p>
    <p>
      Independent means what it says: no sponsor, no syllabus committee, no
      house line to defend. We publish a subject when we can treat it properly,
      and not before.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .intro {
      padding-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .intro h2 {
      font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .intro p {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
